{"name":"Wooden Cabin","hex":"#765a3f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wooden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of wood.","As if made of wood; moving awkwardly, or speaking with dull lack of emotion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wooden"},{"term":"cabin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small dwelling characteristic of the frontier, especially when built from logs with simple tools and not constructed by professional builders, but by those who meant to live in it.","A chalet or lodge, especially one that can hold large groups of people."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To place in a cabin or other small space.","To limit the scope of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Log house","blocks":[{"text":"A log house, or log building, is a structure built with horizontal logs interlocked at the corners by notching. Logs may be round, squared or hewn to other shapes, either handcrafted or milled. The term \"log cabin\" generally refers to a smaller, more rustic log house, such as a hunting cabin in the woods, that may or may not have electricity or plumbing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/S%C3%B8re_Harildstad_n%C3%B8rdre_stu_2.JPG/330px-S%C3%B8re_Harildstad_n%C3%B8rdre_stu_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Log_house"},{"title":"Wood","blocks":[{"text":"Wood is a structural tissue/material found as xylem in the stems and roots of trees and other woody plants. Being a natural material, it is characterized as an organic material – a natural composite of cellulosic fibers that are strong in tension and embedded in a matrix of lignin and hemicelluloses that resists compression."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/16_wood_samples.jpg/330px-16_wood_samples.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&u